  "title": "SupplierCatalogPage Load More pagination appends to existing products instead of replacing",
  "description": "R6 deep audit finding. Dimension: Wiring. Severity: P2. Source SHA: bbd487a3. Scope: R6_DEEP_AUDIT_WAVE. The Load More button (line 329) calls `fetchCatalog(searchTerm || undefined, pagination.offset + pagination.limit)` with the new offset. However, looking at the component behavior, when a search term changes, the offset should reset to 0. If the user has loaded 3 pages (offset=60), then types a new search, the fetchCatalog may be called with offset=0 for the new search, but the state might still show the previously loaded products until the new results arrive, creating a flash of stale data. Additionally, the infinite scroll guard mentioned in the summary needs the fetch to APPEND results (for Load More) rather than REPLACE (for new search), which requires different state update logic.",
